\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Computed Hawking mass and equality for round Schwarzschild sections and identified the asymptotic cancellation scale; general cone limits, Bondi identification and inequality remain.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30003920. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{A round-cone normalization check.} In a spherical exterior take outgoing and ingoing null normals normalized to inner product \(-2\), with expansions \(\theta_+=2/r\), \(\theta_-=-2f(r)/r\). For round sections of area \(A=4\pi r^2\), define
\[
 m_H=\sqrt{A/(16\pi)}\left(1+\frac1{16\pi}\int\theta_+\theta_-\,dA\right).
\]
Since the product is constant on the sphere, substitution gives \(m_H=r(1-f(r))/2\). For \(f(r)=1-2M/r\), the result is exactly \(M\) at every radius. At the round horizon \(r=2M\), it equals \(\sqrt{A/(16\pi)}\), so the expected Penrose relation is an equality in this benchmark.
\paragraph{The cancellation requiring control.} For \(f(r)=1-2M/r+o(r^{-1})\), the same formula gives \(m_H\to M\). Merely assuming \(f(r)=1+o(1)\) would not suffice: \(f=1-r^{-1/2}\) gives \(m_H=\sqrt r/2\). This latter lapse is an asymptotic algebraic countercheck, not an asserted admissible vacuum cone.
\paragraph{Full-scope gap.} General cones have nonconstant expansions, shear and foliation dependence. The exact cancellation of the order-one term in the parentheses must persist with an integrable error, and an asymptotic coefficient must be identified with the correctly normalized Bondi mass. A limit alone also gives no monotonic comparison to the initial area. Proving those geometric estimates and monotonicity under the source hypotheses is the first gap. No foliation-independent limit or general null Penrose inequality is established.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked null normalization and area factors, exact equality at r=2M and a weaker-asymptotics failure without claiming an admissible spacetime counterexample. This is a GPT-6 Astra Ultra self-audit, not independent human verification. Prompt A drafting followed by prompt B scope/dependency/boundary self-audit. Checked null normalization and area factors, exact equality at r=2M and a weaker-asymptotics failure without claiming an admissible spacetime counterexample. The remaining gap is: Control expansion/shear asymptotics and a suitable monotonicity along the actual cone foliation. Unresolved status and zero original-target completion are retained.

Coordinator checked the Hawking-mass substitution, Schwarzschild equality and the asymptotic decay countercheck. General cone monotonicity is not asserted. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

